{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.SouriauModularHamiltonianBridge\nimport InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.OperatorThermodynamics\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.BoundedModularFlowCalibration\n\nWitness-gated bounded modular-flow calibration.\n\nThis file does not construct Tomita--Takesaki modular flow, does not prove a\nKMS theorem, and does not identify a bounded operator with an unbounded\nType-III modular logarithm.  It records the finite/bounded calibration layer:\n\n`K_sur` generates a supplied one-parameter bounded flow, and the Souriau bare\noperator `K̂_β` is the same calibrated generator.  Any KMS-like condition is\nkept as explicit witness data.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.BoundedModularFlowCalibration\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.SouriauModularHamiltonianBridge\nopen InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra.Thermodynamics\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type*}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\nvariable {LieAlgebra : Type*}\n\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => E →L[ℝ] E\n\nnoncomputable local instance boundedModularFlowNormedRing : NormedRing EndH :=\n  inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance boundedModularFlowNormedAlgebra : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH :=\n  inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance boundedModularFlowNormedAlgebraRat : NormedAlgebra ℚ EndH :=\n  NormedAlgebra.restrictScalars ℚ ℝ EndH\nlocal instance boundedModularFlowTopologicalRing : IsTopologicalRing EndH :=\n  inferInstance\nlocal instance boundedModularFlowSMulCommClass : SMulCommClass ℝ EndH EndH :=\n  inferInstance\nlocal instance boundedModularFlowIsScalarTower : IsScalarTower ℝ EndH EndH :=\n  inferInstance\n\n/--\nBounded modular-flow calibration for the Souriau/Drazin surrogate.\n\nThe one-parameter flow and KMS-like law are supplied externally.  The structure\nonly records that the bounded generator is the calibrated Drazin/MP surrogate\n`K_sur`, equivalently the Souriau bare source `K̂_β`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure BoundedModularFlowCalibration where\n  /-- Souriau calibration of the bounded Drazin/supercharge surrogate. -/\n  souriau :\n    SouriauModularHamiltonianBridge (E := E) (LieAlgebra := LieAlgebra)\n\n  /-- Supplied bounded one-parameter flow. -/\n  flow : ℝ → EndH\n\n  /--\n  Ring-level observable modular flow.\n\n  This is the algebraic automorphism surface used for regular-support\n  commutant stability.  It is deliberately separate from `flow : ℝ → EndH`,\n  which is only the bounded one-parameter implementing family.\n  -/\n  modularFlow : ModularFlow EndH\n\n  /--\n  Calibration of the observable modular flow by the bounded adjoint action.\n  Concrete models may replace this witness by a stronger functional-calculus\n  construction.\n  -/\n  modularFlow_eq_bounded_adjoint :\n    ∀ t : ℝ, ∀ A : EndH,\n      modularFlow.flow t A = flow t * A * flow (-t)\n\n  /-- Flow is normalized at zero. -/\n  flow_zero : flow 0 = (1 : EndH)\n\n  /-- Supplied additive/group law for the bounded flow. -/\n  flow_add : ∀ s t : ℝ, flow (s + t) = flow s * flow t\n\n  /-- Calibration: the bounded flow is generated by the Drazin/MP surrogate. -/\n  flow_eq_exp_Ksur :\n    ∀ t : ℝ, flow t = NormedSpace.exp (t • souriau.superBridge.Ksur)\n\n  /--\n  External KMS-like compatibility predicate.  This is deliberately a witness\n  field: this bridge does not prove analytic KMS boundary conditions.\n  -/\n  kmsLikeCompatibility : Prop\n\n  /-- Supplied proof of the bounded KMS-like compatibility predicate. -/\n  kmsLikeCompatibility_holds : kmsLikeCompatibility\n\nnamespace BoundedModularFlowCalibration\n\nvariable (C : BoundedModularFlowCalibration (E := E) (LieAlgebra := LieAlgebra))\n\n/-- Readback of zero-time flow normalization. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_zero_readback :\n    C.flow 0 = (1 : EndH) :=\n  C.flow_zero\n\n/-- Readback of the supplied additive flow law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_add_readback (s t : ℝ) :\n    C.flow (s + t) = C.flow s * C.flow t :=\n  C.flow_add s t\n\n/-- The bounded flow is generated by the Drazin/MP modular-Hamiltonian surrogate. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_eq_exp_Ksur_readback (t : ℝ) :\n    C.flow t = NormedSpace.exp (t • C.souriau.superBridge.Ksur) :=\n  C.flow_eq_exp_Ksur t\n\n/-- The same bounded flow is generated by the Souriau bare source `K̂_β`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem flow_eq_exp_Khat_beta (t : ℝ) :\n    C.flow t = NormedSpace.exp (t • C.souriau.family.Khat_beta) := by\n  rw [C.flow_eq_exp_Ksur_readback t, C.souriau.Khat_beta_eq_Ksur]\n\n/-- Observable modular flow as the supplied bounded adjoint action. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularFlow_eq_bounded_adjoint_readback (t : ℝ) (A : EndH) :\n    C.modularFlow.flow t A = C.flow t * A * C.flow (-t) :=\n  C.modularFlow_eq_bounded_adjoint t A\n\n/-- Ring-level zero-time observable flow normalization. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularFlow_zero_readback (A : EndH) :\n    C.modularFlow.flow 0 A = A :=\n  C.modularFlow.flow_zero A\n\n/-- Ring-level additive observable-flow law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularFlow_add_readback (s t : ℝ) (A : EndH) :\n    C.modularFlow.flow (s + t) A =\n      C.modularFlow.flow s (C.modularFlow.flow t A) :=\n  C.modularFlow.flow_add s t A\n\n/-- Spectral projector used by the Drazin regular sector. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nabbrev spectralProjector : EndH :=\n  C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.spectralProjector\n\n/--\nExternal predicate: the bounded surrogate modular flow fixes the Drazin\nregular projector.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef FlowFixesSpectralProjector : Prop :=\n  ∀ t : ℝ, C.modularFlow.flow t C.spectralProjector = C.spectralProjector\n\n/--\nIf the ring-level modular flow fixes `P_D`, then commutation with `P_D` is\npreserved by the flow.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularFlow_preserves_commuting_with_spectralProjector\n    (hFix : C.FlowFixesSpectralProjector)\n    (A : EndH)\n    (hComm : C.spectralProjector * A = A * C.spectralProjector)\n    (t : ℝ) :\n    C.spectralProjector * C.modularFlow.flow t A =\n      C.modularFlow.flow t A * C.spectralProjector := by\n  let σ := C.modularFlow.flow t\n  calc\n    C.spectralProjector * σ A\n        = σ C.spectralProjector * σ A := by\n            rw [hFix t]\n    _ = σ (C.spectralProjector * A) := by\n            rw [map_mul]\n    _ = σ (A * C.spectralProjector) := by\n            rw [hComm]\n    _ = σ A * σ C.spectralProjector := by\n            rw [map_mul]\n    _ = σ A * C.spectralProjector := by\n            rw [hFix t]\n\n/--\nExternal predicate: the observable modular flow is compatible with the Souriau\nscalar/operator scaling API.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef FlowCommutesWithOpScale : Prop :=\n  ∀ (t : ℝ) (r : ℝ) (A : EndH),\n    C.modularFlow.flow t (C.souriau.family.opScale r A) =\n      C.souriau.family.opScale r (C.modularFlow.flow t A)\n\n/--\nThe Massieu/partition-potential operator shift commutes through the bounded\nobservable modular flow, provided the flow is compatible with Souriau\n`opScale`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem partition_potential_modularFlow_central\n    (hScale : C.FlowCommutesWithOpScale)\n    (t : ℝ) (A : EndH) :\n    C.modularFlow.flow t\n        (C.souriau.family.opScale C.souriau.family.partitionPotential A) =\n      C.souriau.family.opScale C.souriau.family.partitionPotential\n        (C.modularFlow.flow t A) :=\n  hScale t C.souriau.family.partitionPotential A\n\n/--\nThe normalized Souriau modular Hamiltonian remains the bounded surrogate plus\nthe Massieu/free-energy scalar identity term.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem modularHamiltonian_eq_Ksur_add_partitionPotential_one :\n    C.souriau.family.modularHamiltonian =\n      C.souriau.superBridge.Ksur + C.souriau.family.partitionPotential • (1 : EndH) :=\n  C.souriau.modularHamiltonian_eq_Ksur_add_partitionPotential_one\n\n/-- The bounded flow generator is left-supported on the Drazin regular sector. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem spectralProjector_mul_generator :\n    C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.spectralProjector * C.souriau.family.Khat_beta =\n      C.souriau.family.Khat_beta :=\n  C.souriau.spectralProjector_mul_Khat_beta\n\n/-- The bounded flow generator is right-supported on the Drazin regular sector. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_mul_spectralProjector :\n    C.souriau.family.Khat_beta * C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.spectralProjector =\n      C.souriau.family.Khat_beta :=\n  C.souriau.Khat_beta_mul_spectralProjector\n\n/-- The Drazin defect sector annihilates the bounded flow generator on the left. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem spectralComplementaryProjector_mul_generator_eq_zero :\n    C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.spectralComplementaryProjector * C.souriau.family.Khat_beta =\n      0 :=\n  C.souriau.spectralComplementaryProjector_mul_Khat_beta_eq_zero\n\n/-- The Drazin defect sector annihilates the bounded flow generator on the right. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_mul_spectralComplementaryProjector_eq_zero :\n    C.souriau.family.Khat_beta * C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.spectralComplementaryProjector =\n      0 :=\n  C.souriau.Khat_beta_mul_spectralComplementaryProjector_eq_zero\n\n/-- The bounded flow generator is even for the Drazin spectral grading. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_commutes_GammaS :\n    C.souriau.family.Khat_beta * C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.GammaS =\n      C.souriau.superBridge.CIK.GammaS * C.souriau.family.Khat_beta :=\n  C.souriau.Khat_beta_commutes_GammaS\n\n/-- Readback of the supplied KMS-like compatibility witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem kmsLikeCompatibility_readback :\n    C.kmsLikeCompatibility :=\n  C.kmsLikeCompatibility_holds\n\nend BoundedModularFlowCalibration\n\nend Core\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.BoundedModularFlowCalibration\n","mtime":1778711237547}